LATENT DISPATCH
Fri Sep 18 · 5 items · ~4 min

THE CASE FOR BORING AGENTS
Our essay of the week. The agents that are earning their keep in production share three traits: a fixed set of tools (usually under ten), a hard step limit, and a human or a rule between the model and anything irreversible. None of them are impressive in a demo. All of them are still running. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/boring-agents

HALCYON VISION 3.1
Fixes the rotated-page problem from the Ostrava benchmark. Field accuracy on scanned procurement documents goes from 58% to 71% on our re-run. Still not a replacement for validation, but a real step.

NIMBUS OUTAGE: 90 MINUTES, ALL REGIONS
A bad deploy took down the API globally on Wednesday evening. Post-mortem promised. If you were single-provider on Nimbus you felt it; if you had a fallback, your router earned its keep. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/nimbus-outage

SABLE LABS PUBLISHES A PRICING FAQ
Notable for admitting that list prices are negotiable above $50k/year. Everyone knew; nobody had said it in writing.

SHORT TAKES
· Ferrite-8B gets a 1.1 with better JSON adherence.
· Brindle adds a cost budget per run. Pauses the agent, pings a human.
· Vireo-3 now on Kestrel and Argent.

